  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Have that: «I need it.»",
   "texto": [
    "To say «have to» is used **надо + infinitivo**; the person goes in dative: **Мне надо работать** = I have to work (literally, «I need to work.»).",
    "**Тебе надо** = you have to. **Вам надо** can mean you have either you have / have to."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Know how to do",
   "texto": [
    "**Уметь + infinitivo** expresses know how to do or have a skill: **Я умею плавать** (swim), **я умею водить машину** (drive).",
    "**Знать** is to know a data or to know; **уметь** is to have the ability to do something. **Мочь** expresses capacity or possibility in a situation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "It can and cannot.",
